# Eepo-attack.lic
# Bigshot custom attack routine for Eepo (Rogue, two longswords). Drop it into a bigshot
# hunting-commands list as a single command, replacing "surge(!surge s30), attack (xx)":
#
#   script Eepo-attack
#
# bigshot pauses itself, runs this once against the target it already has locked, then
# resumes to loot / wander / retarget -- so this does exactly ONE attack decision per
# call and returns; bigshot re-invokes it every pass while the target is still up. Same
# shape as Fizzlestiks-attack.lic.
#
# Each pass: Surge of Strength first if it isn't already running AND Lich's own
# CMan.available? says it can be used right now (known, 30 stamina, not overexerted --
# no hardcoded stamina number here to drift out of date; that is the old "!surge s30"
# gate), then one plain attack, the way the profile did a surge and then attacks.
# Eepo's only CMan is Surge of Strength 3/5 (11/03), so there is nothing else to weave in.
#
# Written 11/19 from the 11/03 profile line and log (cman surge: "You focus deep within
# yourself..."); NOT run live yet.
#
# Disarm: nothing in the RIGHT hand means a sword is gone. Tries READY WEAPON once; if
# that fails too, asks bigshot to rest instead of punching -- Brayis died doing that.

# --- helpers -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Monster-agnostic death check: bigshot itself never text-matches kill messages --
# it reads GameObj status, which Lich keeps current. "dead" while the corpse lingers,
# "gone" once it decays or is looted.
def target_dead?(foe)
  return true if foe.nil?
  return true if foe.status.to_s =~ /dead|gone/
  !GameObj.targets.any? { |t| t.id.to_i == foe.id.to_i && t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }
end

# Plain attack with whatever is in hand. No-ops if the target is already dead.
def plain_attack(foe)
  return if target_dead?(foe)
  fput "attack"
  waitrt?
end

# Surge of Strength when it isn't already up. CMan.use waits out roundtime first and
# returns the answering line, or nil if it never sent anything.
# @return [Boolean] true if a surge was actually sent
def try_surge
  return false if CMan.buff_active?("surge")
  return false unless CMan.available?("surge")
  !CMan.use("surge").nil?
end

def handle_disarmed
  echo "########## NO WEAPON IN RIGHT HAND -- not fighting bare-fisted ##########"
  echo "## asking bigshot to rest"
  $bigshot_should_rest = true
  $rest_reason = "Disarmed"
end

# --- main ----------------------------------------------------------------

foe = GameObj.targets.find { |t| t.id.to_i == XMLData.current_target_id.to_i } if XMLData.current_target_id
foe ||= GameObj.targets.find { |t| t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }

# nothing (live) to hit -- hand control straight back to bigshot, which loots
exit if target_dead?(foe)

fput "target ##{foe.id}" unless XMLData.current_target_id.to_i == foe.id.to_i

waitrt?

exit if target_dead?(foe)

if checkright.nil?
  fput "ready weapon"
  pause 0.5
  if checkright.nil?
    handle_disarmed
    exit
  end
end

fput "stance offensive" if stance != "offensive"

try_surge
exit if target_dead?(foe)
plain_attack(foe)
